AudioFlinger: Let Bluetooth outputs idle after the usual delay

The Echo Dot keeps its speaker output out of standby with a long
ro.audio.flinger_standbytime_ms, since every standby switches its
amplifier off and the next sound pops when it comes back on. The same
delay applied to Bluetooth outputs, which then streamed silence to
headphones and speakers for as long as they stayed connected.

Give A2DP outputs the default standby delay whatever the property says.
A thread caches its delay when its loop starts, before its first audio
patch sets the device, so work the delay out again whenever a patch
changes a mixer thread's device.

diff --git a/services/audioflinger/Threads.cpp b/services/audioflinger/Threads.cpp
--- a/services/audioflinger/Threads.cpp
+++ b/services/audioflinger/Threads.cpp
@@ -3211,11 +3211,18 @@
 
     // make sure standby delay is not too short when connected to an A2DP sink to avoid
     // truncating audio when going to standby.
+    updateStandbyDelay_l();
+}
+
+void AudioFlinger::PlaybackThread::updateStandbyDelay_l()
+{
     mStandbyDelayNs = AudioFlinger::mStandbyTimeInNsecs;
     if (!Intersection(outDeviceTypes(),  getAudioDeviceOutAllA2dpSet()).empty()) {
-        if (mStandbyDelayNs < kDefaultStandbyTimeInNsecs) {
-            mStandbyDelayNs = kDefaultStandbyTimeInNsecs;
-        }
+        // A device that keeps its speaker out of standby with a long
+        // ro.audio.flinger_standbytime_ms still lets Bluetooth headphones
+        // and speakers idle after the usual delay, instead of streaming
+        // silence to them for as long as they stay connected.
+        mStandbyDelayNs = kDefaultStandbyTimeInNsecs;
     }
 }
 
@@ -4242,6 +4249,12 @@
                          (mPatch.sinks[0].id != sinkPortId);
     mPatch = *patch;
     mOutDeviceTypeAddrs = deviceTypeAddrs;
+    // The thread cached its standby delay before its first patch set the
+    // device, so a Bluetooth output kept the delay of any other output.
+    // Direct and offload threads set their own delays.
+    if (mType == MIXER) {
+        updateStandbyDelay_l();
+    }
     checkSilentMode_l();
 
     if (mOutput->audioHwDev->supportsAudioPatches()) {
